CORE broken-libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp20 --unwind 6
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* iota: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* transform: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* filter: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* drop: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
g++ 13 (-fsanitize=address,undefined) and clang++ 18 accept this program,
and it fails only its WRONG assertion.
broken-libstdcxx16: with libstdc++ 16, std::__invoke and __invoke_impl of
the views::transform and views::filter range adaptor closures lose their
bodies (KNOWNBUG cpp20_range_adaptor_closure_invoked_through_invoke_impl).
